=== Ablated Response (multiplier=0.0) ===
 Frida Kahlo was a renowned Mexican artist known for her self-portraits and works that often depicted themes of pain, identity, and the human experience. Born on July 6, 1900, in Coyoacán, Mexico City, she was deeply influenced by various aspects of her life, including her Tehuana heritage, her tumultuous relationship with fellow artist Diego Rivera, and her physical suffering due to polio as a child and a bus accident later in life.

Kahlo's work blended elements from European painting techniques with traditional Mexican folk art. Despite her relatively short career ( she died in 1954 at age 47), her influence has grown significantly since her death. Today, she is considered one of the most important figures in 20nd century art, and her works are displayed in major museums around the world. Notable collections include those at the Museo de Arte Moderno in Mexico City and the Art Institute of Chicago. Her life story has also been adapted into several biographical films and books.

